				<r3d:description language="eng">The Tropospheric Ozone Assessment Report (TOAR) database of  global surface observations is the world&#039;s most extensive collection of surface ozone measurements and includes also data on other air pollutants and  on weather for some regions. Measurements from 1970 to 2019 (Version 1) have been collected in a relational database, and are made available via a graphical web interface, a REST service (https://toar-data.fz-juelich.de/api/v1) and as aggregated products on PANGAEA (https://doi.pangaea.de/10.1594/PANGAEA.876108). Measurements from 1970 to present (Version 2) are being collected in a relational database, and are made available via a REST service (https://toar-data.fz-juelich.de/api/v2).</r3d:description>
